---
import Article from '../../layouts/Article.astro';
import CompareTable from '../../components/compare/CompareTable.astro';
import Cite from '../../components/compare/Cite.astro';
import MoveCode from '../../components/compare/MoveCode.astro';
import Related from '../../components/compare/Related.astro';
import Sources from '../../components/compare/Sources.astro';
import { S } from '../../components/compare/siar';
import { RIVALS, CHECKED, citeHtml } from '../../data/rivals';
import { OPENAPI_LINE } from '../../lib/status';

const r = RIVALS.metricool;
const x = r.facts;
const c = r.cells;

const faq = [
  { q: 'Which Metricool plan includes the API?', a: 'Advanced and Custom. Metricool says its Free and Starter plans do not include API access. Advanced starts at $67 a month, or $53 a month billed yearly.' + citeHtml(x.gate) },
  { q: 'Does Siar charge per X account?', a: "No. Siar has no per-account fees. X posts are paid from a prepaid credit at X's own USD prices." },
];
---
<Article
  metaTitle="Metricool API alternative on every plan | Siar"
  h1="Metricool API alternative: the API on every plan, with signed webhooks"
  description="Metricool's API starts on Advanced at $67 a month, with no webhooks. Siar is a unified social media API on every plan, with signed webhooks and a connect link."
  kicker="Compare"
  updated={CHECKED}
  crumbs={[{ name: 'Compare', href: '/compare' }, { name: 'Metricool API alternative', href: '/compare/metricool-api' }]}
  lead={`Metricool's API starts on its Advanced plan, at $67 a month, and sends no webhooks. Siar, a unified social media API, includes the API on every plan, from ${S.freeStart} to ${S.starterUsd} a month (${S.starterMyr} in Malaysia). Your customers connect their accounts through your branded link, and every webhook is signed.`}
  actions="quickstart"
  faq={faq}
>
  <CompareTable rival={r} />

  <h2 id="where-metricool-wins">Where Metricool is the better choice</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>You want a hosted MCP server, free.</strong> Metricool's is {c.mcp!.value.toLowerCase()} (<Cite f={c.mcp!} />). Siar's is not hosted: {S.tooling}</li>
    <li><strong>Analytics and ads come first.</strong> Metricool covers ad platforms and deep reporting (<Cite f={c.networks!} />). Siar has account and post analytics on paid plans, and no ads.</li>
    <li><strong>You need TikTok, YouTube, Pinterest or Google Business Profile.</strong> Metricool lists them. On Siar: {S.tiktok} {S.pinterest} {S.youtube}</li>
    <li><strong>You only schedule for yourself.</strong> {x.freePlan.value} (<Cite f={x.freePlan} />).</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="api-pricing">Metricool API pricing</h2>
  <p>{x.gate.value} (<Cite f={x.gate} />). The lowest plan with the API is Advanced: {c.entry!.value.replace(/^.*The API starts on Advanced: /, '')} (<Cite f={c.entry!} />). X costs extra: {x.xAddon.value.charAt(0).toLowerCase() + x.xAddon.value.slice(1)} (<Cite f={x.xAddon} />).</p>
  <p>Metricool bills per brand, with one profile per network in each brand. Siar's unit is close: each brand connects one account on every open network, with no per-account fees. The difference is the bill: Siar Pro is {S.proUsd} a month for {S.proBrands}, with the API included.</p>

  <h2 id="what-siar-adds">What Siar adds for a product that publishes for its customers</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>The API on every plan.</strong> Free included, with {S.freeStart}.</li>
    <li><strong>A connect link on every plan.</strong> Metricool's connect-link API is for integrators on its Custom plan (<Cite f={c.connect!} />).</li>
    <li><strong>Signed webhooks.</strong> Siar signs each webhook and retries it for about 45 hours. Metricool's API description has no outbound webhooks (<Cite f={c.webhooks!} />).</li>
    <li><strong>Mastodon, Discord and Slack</strong> are open on Siar today.</li>
    <li><strong>One designed contract.</strong> {OPENAPI_LINE()}</li>
  </ul>
  <p>{S.priceLock}</p>

  <MoveCode>
    <p>Metricool brands map to Siar brands one to one. In the API a brand is a team. Send each client a connect link instead of connecting their profiles inside your Metricool account. Scheduled posts become one Siar post with a payload per network, and polling for results becomes a webhook subscription.</p>
  </MoveCode>

  <Related />
  <Sources rivals={[r]} />
</Article>
